  "articleBody": "Great kitchen task lighting makes a huge difference in how enjoyable and safe your cooking and prep spaces are. The trick is to get enough light directly onto your work surfaces without casting shadows from your own body. You want to avoid placing lights too far back under cabinets, as this is a common mistake that leaves your body blocking the light precisely where you need it. Consider the lumen output; for task areas, you'll need brighter lights than for ambient lighting. Think about color temperature too – a cooler white light (around 4000K) is often preferred for tasks as it helps with visibility and accuracy. Don't forget about dimming compatibility, so you can adjust the brightness for different activities. When planning, always think about where your fixtures will be placed over the work zone and ensure your existing electrical box or circuit can handle the load. If you're looking to upgrade your kitchen task lighting and need new wiring or circuit changes, that’s definitely a job for a qualified professional to ensure everything is up to code and safe. At HH Remodeling LLC, we can help you integrate effective lighting solutions into your kitchen remodel.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}